    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d355">

                <pb facs="0470" n="402" xml:id="pg402"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72/1757½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-05-13">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">13 May, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>My Dear Mr. Secretary: After sleeping over your suggestion, I have this to
                    propose:</p>
                <p>It would not be wise, I think, to give out a direct statement; but I think the
                    same purpose would be served by such a “tip” as the enclosed, accompanying the
                    publication of the note. And it would be best that this tip should be given out
                    from the Executive Office, while the note was given out by the Department of
                    State. What do you think?</p>
                <p>If you will return the paper in the course of the morning, I will make the
                    necessary arrangements.</p>
                <p>Faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W.</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d355-a1.xml" xpointer="d355-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
